        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void VERUM_AUX_MEMORY_16B_copy</definition>
        <argsstring>(void *restrict destination, const void *restrict source)</argsstring>
        <name>VERUM_AUX_MEMORY_16B_copy</name>
        <param>
          <type>void *restrict</type>
          <declname>destination</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const void *restrict</type>
          <declname>source</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Copy exactly 128 bits (16 bytes) from <computeroutput>source</computeroutput> to <computeroutput>destination</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Fixed-width specialisation for 128-bit block transfers. Both pointers must be 4-byte aligned and must not overlap. Emits exactly four word-width loads and four word-width stores with no branching or runtime alignment probing.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">destination</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target buffer. Must be 4-byte aligned. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">source</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Source buffer. Must be 4-byte aligned.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>destination</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>source</computeroutput> are non-NULL. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para>Both pointers are aligned to <computeroutput>sizeof(uint32_t)</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para>The regions [<computeroutput>destination</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>destination</computeroutput> + 16) and [<computeroutput>source</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>source</computeroutput> + 16) do not overlap. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
